<title>USA: Hitachi PC to use Intel MMX chip.</title>
<headline>Hitachi PC to use Intel MMX chip.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Calif. 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hitachi PC Corp, a unit of Japanese electronics maker Hitachi Ltd, on Monday said it will use Intel Corp's new 133 megahertz Pentium microprocessor with the MMX multimedia technology in its future corporate- and value-line notebook computer products.</p>
<p>&quot;This new chip will provide cost-conscious mobile computer users a high level of processing power when utilizing intensive multimedia and communications applications,&quot; Mark Yahiro, vice president of marketing and business development for Hitachi PC, said in a statement.</p>
</text>
